============================================================
1. HIGH-LEVEL OVERVIEW
============================================================
Components:
- Frontend: React SPA
- Backend API: FastAPI
- Database: Postgres
- Cache/Queue: Redis
- Workers: Celery
- Cluster: K3s (self-hosted)
- Packaging: Helm charts
- Ingress: HTTP(S) reverse proxy
- Storage: Persistent Volumes (PV/PVC)

All services run inside the K3s cluster, exposed via Ingress.


============================================================
2. ENVIRONMENTS
============================================================
- production: live council site
- staging: pre-production testing
- dev: local or shared development

Each environment has:
- its own namespace
- its own database
- its own Redis instance
- its own ingress routes


============================================================
3. K3s CLUSTER LAYOUT
============================================================

NAMESPACES
----------
- koc-frontend
- koc-backend
- koc-workers
- koc-database
- koc-monitoring

NODES
-----
- master/control-plane node
- 1+ worker nodes for:
  - API
  - frontend
  - workers
  - monitoring

NETWORKING
----------
- CNI plugin for pod networking
- NetworkPolicies to restrict cross-namespace traffic


============================================================
4. HELM CHARTS
============================================================

CHARTS
------
- koc-frontend-chart
- koc-backend-chart
- koc-workers-chart
- koc-postgres-chart
- koc-redis-chart
- koc-monitoring-chart (Prometheus/Grafana)

VALUES
------
- values.yaml per environment
- Override:
  - image tags
  - replica counts
  - resource limits
  - secrets references
  - ingress hosts


============================================================
5. FRONTEND (REACT) DEPLOYMENT
============================================================

ARTIFACT
--------
- Built React app (static files)
- Served by:
  - Nginx container OR
  - Node-based static server

DEPLOYMENT
----------
- Deployment in koc-frontend namespace
- 2–3 replicas (horizontal scaling)
- Config via ConfigMap:
  - API base URL
  - environment flags

INGRESS
-------
- Route: https://council.example.org/
- Path: /
- TLS enabled


============================================================
6. BACKEND (FASTAPI) DEPLOYMENT
============================================================

ARTIFACT
--------
- FastAPI app container
- Gunicorn/Uvicorn workers

DEPLOYMENT
----------
- Deployment in koc-backend namespace
- 2–4 replicas
- Autoscaling based on CPU/RAM

SERVICE
-------
- ClusterIP service: koc-backend-svc
- Exposed internally to:
  - frontend
  - workers

INGRESS
-------
- Route: https://council.example.org/api
- Path: /api
- TLS enabled

CONFIG
------
- Environment variables:
  - DATABASE_URL
  - REDIS_URL
  - JWT_SECRET
  - LOG_LEVEL
- Mounted via ConfigMap + Secret


============================================================
7. DATABASE (POSTGRES) DEPLOYMENT
============================================================

DEPLOYMENT
----------
- StatefulSet in koc-database namespace
- Single primary instance (optionally HA)
- PVC for data:
  - StorageClass: fast-ssd or equivalent
  - Size: e.g., 50–200 GB

SERVICE
-------
- ClusterIP service: koc-postgres-svc
- Accessible only from:
  - backend namespace
  - workers namespace

BACKUPS
-------
- Scheduled backup job (CronJob)
- Store backups in:
  - NFS
  - S3-compatible storage
- Encrypted backups


============================================================
8. REDIS DEPLOYMENT
============================================================

DEPLOYMENT
----------
- Deployment or StatefulSet in koc-backend or koc-workers namespace
- Single instance or small cluster

SERVICE
-------
- ClusterIP service: koc-redis-svc
- Used by:
  - FastAPI (cache, sessions)
  - Celery (broker, backend)

PERSISTENCE
-----------
- Optional PVC for persistence
- Or in-memory only for non-critical data


============================================================
9. CELERY WORKERS DEPLOYMENT
============================================================

DEPLOYMENT
----------
- Deployment in koc-workers namespace
- Separate worker groups:
  - email-worker
  - media-worker
  - voting-worker
  - audit-worker

SCALING
-------
- Horizontal scaling based on:
  - queue length
  - CPU usage

CONFIG
------
- REDIS_URL
- DATABASE_URL (read/write)
- LOG_LEVEL

QUEUE BINDING
-------------
- Each worker subscribes to specific queues:
  - email_queue
  - media_queue
  - voting_queue
  - audit_queue


============================================================
10. INGRESS & ROUTING
============================================================

INGRESS CONTROLLER
------------------
- Nginx or Traefik
- TLS termination
- HTTP → HTTPS redirect

ROUTES
------
- /           → frontend service
- /api        → backend service
- /media      → backend or dedicated media service

SECURITY
--------
- HSTS enabled
- Rate limiting for /api
- IP restrictions for admin endpoints (optional)


============================================================
11. SECRETS & CONFIGURATION
============================================================

SECRETS
-------
- Stored in Kubernetes Secrets
- Managed via:
  - sealed-secrets (GitOps)
- Examples:
  - DATABASE_PASSWORD
  - JWT_SECRET
  - REDIS_PASSWORD

CONFIGMAPS
----------
- Non-sensitive config:
  - API base URLs
  - log levels
  - feature flags

ENV VARS
--------
- Injected from Secrets/ConfigMaps
- No hardcoded secrets in images


============================================================
12. SCALING & HIGH AVAILABILITY
============================================================

SCALING
-------
- Frontend: scale based on requests
- Backend: scale based on CPU/RAM
- Workers: scale based on queue length

HIGH AVAILABILITY
-----------------
- Multiple replicas for:
  - frontend
  - backend
  - workers
- Optional HA for Postgres (read replicas, failover)
- Ingress controller in HA mode


============================================================
13. MONITORING & LOGGING INTEGRATION
============================================================

MONITORING
----------
- Prometheus for metrics
- Grafana for dashboards
- Alerts for:
  - pod restarts
  - high error rates
  - slow responses
  - worker backlog

LOGGING
-------
- Centralized logging (Loki/ELK)
- All pods send logs to aggregator
- Structured JSON logs


============================================================
14. CI/CD PIPELINE
============================================================

PIPELINE STAGES
---------------
1. Build:
   - React app
   - FastAPI image
   - Worker image
2. Test:
   - Unit + integration tests
3. Package:
   - Helm charts
4. Deploy:
   - Staging via Helm
   - Manual approval
   - Production via Helm

ROLLBACK
--------
- Helm rollback on failure
- DB migrations reversible via Alembic


============================================================
15. SECURITY BOUNDARIES
============================================================

BOUNDARIES
----------
- Public internet → Ingress → frontend/backend
- Backend → DB via internal service only
- Workers → DB/Redis via internal services
- No direct DB access from frontend
- Admin endpoints protected by RBAC + HTTPS

NETWORK POLICIES
----------------
- Restrict DB access to backend/workers
- Restrict Redis access to backend/workers
- Restrict cross-namespace traffic


============================================================
16. DISASTER RECOVERY
============================================================

BACKUPS
-------
- Regular DB backups
- Configuration backups (Helm values, manifests)

RESTORE
-------
- Restore DB from backup
- Redeploy services via Helm
- Recreate secrets from sealed-secrets

TESTING
-------
- Periodic DR drills
- Verify backup integrity
